{"text": "Dorothy L, Cheney, a renowned American biologist. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Is famous for her research on social relationships. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Of non human primates like vervet monkeys and baboons. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Born in Boston in 1950. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> She graduated from Wellesley College in 1972. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Although she originally planned to go to law school. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Her career plan changed. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> After she joined her husband, Robert Seyfarth. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> For fieldwork on animal behavior. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Subsequently, she earned a doctoral degree in zoology. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> From Cambridge University. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Between 1977 and 1988. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> She conducted field research in Kenya. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Discovering that vervet monkeys used different alarm calls. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> For different predators such as leopards and snakes. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Afterward, she carried out a project on baboons. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> In Botswana. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Cheney and her husband wrote Baboon Metaphysics. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Describing results from their fieldwork. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Cheney had a strong influence. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> On researchers of animal behavior. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> And many graduate students she mentored. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Went on to distinguished careers in animal behavior.", "alignment": {"characters": ["D", "o", "r", "o", "t", "h", "y", " ", "L", ",", " ", "C", "h", "e", "n", "e", "y", ",", " ", "a", " ", "r", "e", "n", "o", "w", "n", "e", "d", " ", "A", "m", "e", "r", "i", "c", "a", "n", " ", "b", "i", "o", "l", "o", "g", "i", "s", "t", ".", " ", "<", "b", "r", "e", "a", "k", " ", "t", "i", "m", "e", "=", "\"", "0", ".", "8", "s", "\"", " ", "/", ">", " ", "I", "s", " ", "f", "a", "m", "o", "u", "s", " ", "f", "o", "r", " ", "h", "e", "r", " ", "r", "e", "s", "e", "a",